# Line endings.
#
# Shell scripts must be checked out with LF on every platform. Git for Windows
# defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites them to CRLF on checkout — and
# a CRLF shebang fails as:
#
#     bash: ./run.sh: /usr/bin/env bash^M: bad interpreter
#
# which reads as "the script is missing or broken" while the file looks
# perfect in an editor. Anyone on WSL or Git Bash hits it, and nothing on
# screen points at the cause.
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.bash          text eol=lf

# PowerShell is fine either way, but pinning it keeps diffs clean.
*.ps1           text eol=crlf

# Everything else: normalise in the repository, native on checkout.
*.py            text
*.js            text
*.css           text
*.html          text
*.md            text
*.json          text
*.txt           text

# Binary — never touch these.
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.pdf           binary
*.docx          binary
*.xlsx          binary
*.pptx          binary
